     "page": 1,
     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Thomas Valdez and Vasquez Medical Group\nPatient: Scott Wright DOB: 01/21/1995 Sex: M MRN: 783237\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-02-27 Atrial fibrillation / flutter BP 129/92 Wt 129\n 2023-09-20 Atrial fibrillation / flutter BP 143/92 Wt 130\n 2022-04-11 Atrial fibrillation / flutter BP 142/88 Wt 133\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • AFib (normal echo; CHA2DS2-VASc 3; ablation 9.1 yrs ago; 14 yrs since onset) - controlled; meds: metoprolol 50 mg\n\nSocial History:\n Tobacco: Former cigarette smoker at 1 pack per day. Quit smoking on June 7, 2025. Patient reported honest disclosure.\n\nChief Complaints:\n Patient presented with complaints of occasional palpitations and fatigue. He denies chest pain, syncope, or dizziness.\n\nReview of Systems:\n - Cardiovascular: Reports occasional palpitations. Denies chest pain, syncope, or shortness of breath.\n - Respiratory: No cough, wheezing, or shortness of breath.\n - Neurological: No headaches, dizziness, or syncope.\n - Gastrointestinal: No nausea, vomiting, or abdominal pain.\n - Genitourinary: No dysuria or hematuria.\n - Musculoskeletal: No joint pain or muscle weakness.\n - Endocrine: No excessive thirst or hunger.\n - Psychiatric: No depressive or anxiety.\n\nPhysical Examination:\n - General: Alert, oriented x3, in no acute distress.\n - Vitals: BP 129/92, HR 78, RR 16, Temp 98.6°F, Wt 129 lb, BMI 20.3\n - Cardiovascular: Regular rhythm, no murmurs, clicks, or gallops. Palpable apical impulse. No edema.\n - Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.\n - Neurological: Cranial nerves II-XII intact. Motor and sensory intact. Reflexes 2+ and symmetric.\n - Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, no organomegaly.\n - Extremities: No cyanosis, clubbing, or edema.\n - Skin: No lesions or rashes.\n\nDiagnostic Tests:\n - Echocardiogram: Normal ejection fraction, normal left ventricular size and function.\n - EKG: Atrial fibrillation controlled ventricular rate.\n - Lab Results:\n - Complete Blood Count (CBC): WNL\n - Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP): WNL\n - Thyroid Function Tests: WNL\n - BNP: Within normal limits\n\nManagement Plan:\n - Continue metoprolol 50 mg daily for rate control.\n - Patient educated on signs of AFib exacerbation and importance of medication adherence.\n - follow-up in 3 months for routine monitoring of AFib.\n - Recommend regular follow-ups with cardiology for ongoing management.\n\nDr. Sandra Smith, Cardiologist\nThomas Valdez and Vasquez Medical Group\nDate: 2025-03-01\n\nThis summary\n"
